---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
<Fragment slot="head">
<meta name="description" content="Build a simple small business website with AI and own it forever. Free single file HTML templates, a prompt builder, honest tool recommendations, and free hosting guides. No subscriptions, no lock-in.">
<title>BlueYucca | Free HTML Website Templates You Own Forever</title>
<link rel="canonical" href="https://blueyucca.com/">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="BlueYucca">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="BlueYucca | Free HTML Website Templates You Own Forever">
<meta property="og:description" content="Build a simple small business website with AI and own it forever. Free templates, a prompt builder, honest tool recommendations, and free hosting guides. No subscriptions, no lock-in.">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://blueyucca.com/">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<style is:inline>
  :root {
    --cream: #FAF6ED; --cream-deep: #F3ECDC; --card: #FFFDF8;
    --sand: #E5DAC3; --sand-dark: #D5C6A5;
    --ink: #1E2A45; --ink-soft: #52607E;
    --blue: #2455C4; --blue-deep: #17357F; --blue-dark: #1B3A8C;
    --blue-soft: #4B79DC; --blue-wash: #E9EFFB; --blue-line: #C9D8F5;
    --haz: #F2C94C;
    --mono: "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    background: var(--cream); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.65;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  ::selection { background: var(--blue); color: var(--cream); }
  a { color: var(--blue); }
  .wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(22px); transition: opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease; }
  .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
    html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
  }
  header.site {
    position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 50;
    background: rgba(250,246,237,0.88);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .nav { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 13px 24px; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .brand {
    font-weight: 900; font-size: 1.45rem; color: var(--blue-deep);
    text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    transform: rotate(-2deg); display: inline-block;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--sand); transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }
  .brand:hover { transform: rotate(1deg) scale(1.04); }
  .brand .b1 { color: var(--blue); } .brand .b2 { color: var(--ink); }
  .nav-links { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .nav-links a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .nav-links a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .nav-cta {
    background: var(--blue); color: var(--cream) !important;
    padding: 8px 16px; border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink); font-weight: 800 !important;
    transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
  }
  .nav-cta:hover { transform: translate(1px, 1px); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .nav-links { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.9rem; } }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--cream); padding: 4px 10px;
    transform: rotate(-1deg); margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .hero { padding: 72px 0 30px; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.4vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-weight: 900; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .hero .lede { font-size: 1.18rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .btn-row { display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 13px 22px; border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink);
    transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
  }
  .btn:hover { transform: translate(2px, 2px); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--blue); color: var(--cream); }
  .btn.secondary { background: var(--card); color: var(--ink); }


  .quick-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin: 40px 0 20px; }
  .quick {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 18px;
  }
  .quick strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .quick p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .quick:nth-child(odd) { transform: rotate(-0.4deg); }
  .quick:nth-child(even) { transform: rotate(0.4deg); }

  section.block { padding: 54px 0 10px; }
  .kicker { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue-deep); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  section.block h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.6vw, 2.3rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  section.block .sub { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 26px; }

  .datechip {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    background: var(--haz); color: var(--ink); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 3px 9px; transform: rotate(-1deg); margin-left: 10px; vertical-align: middle;
  }

  .current-note {
    background: var(--blue-wash); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--ink); padding: 24px 26px; margin: 44px 0 8px;
  }
  .current-note .kicker { color: var(--blue-deep); }
  .current-note p { color: var(--ink); max-width: 760px; }
  .current-note p + p { margin-top: 10px; }

  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 22px; margin-top: 10px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .col { border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 24px; background: var(--card); }
  .col.them { background: var(--cream-deep); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); }
  .col.us { background: var(--card); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--blue); }
  .col .tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .col.us .tag { color: var(--blue-deep); }
  .col h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .col ul { list-style: none; }
  .col li { padding: 7px 0 7px 26px; position: relative; font-size: 0.97rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .col.them li::before { content: "\2717"; position: absolute; left: 2px; color: #B0483C; font-weight: 700; }
  .col.us li::before { content: "\2713"; position: absolute; left: 2px; color: var(--blue); font-weight: 700; }

  .steps-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .step-card { background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 22px; }
  .step-num { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--blue-deep); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .step-card h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 6px 0 8px; }
  .step-card p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .chipbar {
    margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--cream); padding: 8px 10px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .chipbar .live { color: #7CFC9A; font-weight: 700; }

  .tool-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .tool-card { background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 22px; position: relative; }
  .tool-card.featured { box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--blue); }
  .tool-card h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .tool-card p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .tool-card .status {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue-deep);
  }
  .tool-card .go { font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; }
  .sticker {
    position: absolute; top: -12px; right: 12px;
    background: var(--haz); border: 2px solid var(--ink); font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; padding: 3px 8px;
    transform: rotate(3deg);
  }


  .post-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .post-card {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  }
  .post-card .pdate { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .post-card h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .post-card h3 a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
  .post-card h3 a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .post-card p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); flex: 1; }
  .post-card .read { font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 12px; }

  .why { background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--blue); padding: 30px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .why p { max-width: 760px; color: var(--ink); }
  .why p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  mark { background: var(--haz); padding: 1px 5px; }

  .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .stat { border: 2px solid var(--ink); background: var(--card); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 22px; }
  .stat .big { font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 900; color: var(--blue-deep); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .stat strong { display: block; margin-top: 4px; }
  .stat p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  details {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--sand-dark); margin-bottom: 14px; padding: 0;
  }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 800; padding: 16px 20px; list-style: none; }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary::after { content: "+"; float: right; font-weight: 900; color: var(--blue); }
  details[open] summary::after { content: "\2212"; }
  details p { padding: 0 20px 18px; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 28px; align-items: start; margin-top: 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .about-main p { color: var(--ink); max-width: 640px; }
  .about-main p + p, .about-main h3 + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .about-main h3 { margin-top: 22px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .funfact {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 22px; transform: rotate(0.6deg);
  }
  .funfact .tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-weight: 700; background: var(--haz); border: 2px solid var(--ink); display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .funfact h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .funfact p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .whois { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 12px; }

  .cta-final { text-align: center; padding: 70px 0 60px; }
  .cta-final h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin-bottom: 12px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .cta-final p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .cta-final .btn-row { justify-content: center; }

  .site-footer { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); background: var(--cream-deep); padding: 30px 0 40px; margin-top: 30px; text-align: center; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .site-footer nav { margin: 14px 0; }
  .site-footer a { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .site-footer a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .retro-badge {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; background: var(--ink); color: #7CFC9A;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 5px 12px; transform: rotate(-1deg);
  }
</style>
</Fragment>
<header class="site">
  <div class="nav">
    <a class="brand" href="/"><span class="b1">Blue</span><span class="b2">Yucca</span></a>
    <nav class="nav-links">
      <a href="/examples">Examples</a>
      <a href="/prompt-builder">Prompt Builder</a>
      <a href="#tools">Tools</a>
      <a href="/hosting">Hosting Guide</a>
      <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
      <a class="nav-cta" href="/prompt-builder">Start building</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">

  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free and open source</span>
    <h1>Build a simple website.<br>Own it forever.</h1>
    <p class="lede">BlueYucca is free help for everyday business owners and creators: tools, honest recommendations, and plain guides for building fast HTML websites you actually own. No subscriptions, no lock-in, no surprise price hikes. Just files you control.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/prompt-builder">Build your prompt</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="/examples">See the templates</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="quick-grid reveal">
    <div class="quick"><strong>$0 and no account</strong><p>Nothing to sign up for, ever</p></div>
    <div class="quick"><strong>Single HTML files</strong><p>Open them, read them, change them</p></div>
    <div class="quick"><strong>Works with any AI</strong><p>Claude, ChatGPT, or Gemini</p></div>
    <div class="quick"><strong>Host anywhere</strong><p>Free or nearly free, your choice</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="current-note reveal">
    <div class="kicker">A note on staying current</div>
    <p>AI is changing fast. Tools that matter today can be obsolete by next month. Some of them were obsolete last month and nobody told them yet. So everything on this site carries a last reviewed date. If a date looks old, <a href="/contact">ask me about it</a>.</p>
    <p>The goal is not to have the most tools. The goal is to point you at the ones that actually work right now.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="block" id="today">
    <div class="kicker">What works today</div>
    <h2>The free website prompt builder. <span class="datechip">Reviewed Jul 2026</span></h2>
    <p class="sub">This is the fastest way I know today to get a real website you own. Answer some questions, get a prompt, paste it into the AI of your choice, and you get clean HTML with no subscription attached.</p>
    <div class="why reveal">
      <p>One year ago this approach produced websites I would not show anyone. Today it builds sites I am proud of in about an hour. That pace of change is exactly why I keep testing other options, and why this page has a date on it.</p>
      <p><a class="btn primary" href="/prompt-builder" style="margin-top:6px;">Try the prompt builder</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="tools">
    <div class="kicker">The tools list</div>
    <h2>Short list. Actually tested. <span class="datechip">Opening Aug 2026</span></h2>
    <p class="sub">A curated list of tools for running a small business website: forms, payments, email, and more. Every tool on it passes one test: I would run my own business on it. Most of them, I already have.</p>
    <div class="tool-cards">
      <div class="tool-card featured">
        <span class="sticker">IN USE HERE</span>
        <h3>Contact forms</h3>
        <p>The form on this very site runs on the first pick. Tested by using it, not by reading about it.</p>
        <span class="status">First writeups: August</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <h3>Getting paid</h3>
        <p>Simple ways to take payment from a plain HTML page, including a couple of options most lists never mention.</p>
        <span class="status">In testing now</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <h3>Email and more</h3>
        <p>Staying in touch with customers without renting another platform. Plus the tools I use to keep sites fast and findable.</p>
        <span class="status">In testing now</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:22px;">Make a tool that works outside the big platforms? <a href="/contact">I want to hear from you.</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">The difference</div>
    <h2>Renting a website vs. owning one.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Website builders make the first month easy and the years after expensive. BlueYucca starts you on the other path.</p>
    <div class="compare reveal">
      <div class="col them">
        <div class="tag">On a platform</div>
        <h3>Your site lives in their system.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The features you need next always sit in a higher plan</li>
          <li>Your words and photos held inside their editor</li>
          <li>Leaving means starting over from nothing</li>
          <li>The rules can change any time they like</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col us">
        <div class="tag">With BlueYucca</div>
        <h3>Your site is a file you keep.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Pay nothing, or a few dollars for hosting you pick</li>
          <li>Everything lives in plain HTML files on your computer</li>
          <li>Move hosts any afternoon without losing a thing</li>
          <li>Hand your files to any helper, human or AI</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">How it works</div>
    <h2>Three steps. That is the whole system.</h2>
    <p class="sub">No tech background needed at any point.</p>
    <div class="steps-grid reveal">
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">01 SEE</div>
        <h3>Browse the templates</h3>
        <p>Real examples and free templates. Every one is a single HTML file you can open, read, and change. <a href="/examples">Look around</a>.</p>
        <div class="chipbar">yourbusiness.com</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">02 BUILD</div>
        <h3>Describe your business</h3>
        <p>The prompt builder turns plain words into a clear prompt for Claude, ChatGPT, or Gemini. <a href="/prompt-builder">Try it</a>.</p>
        <div class="chipbar">A one page site for my landscaping business in Mesa...</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">03 PUBLISH</div>
        <h3>Put it online</h3>
        <p>Free or nearly free, step by step, no tech background needed. <a href="/hosting">Follow the guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="chipbar">yourbusiness.com <span class="live">LIVE</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">What's next</div>
    <h2>More in the pipeline.</h2>
    <div class="why reveal">
      <p>I am testing tools that could make this whole process even simpler. Some are close. None are ready. When one earns a spot here, it will show up with a date and an honest writeup, same as everything else.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="blog">
    <div class="kicker">From the blog</div>
    <h2>Written by a person who lived it.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Plain talk from twenty plus years of building websites and running small businesses. About one new post a month.</p>
    <div class="post-cards reveal">
      <div class="post-card">
        <div class="pdate">Field notes</div>
        <h3><a href="/blog/building-websites-with-ai">Building websites with AI: what hours of real use taught me</a></h3>
        <p>ChatGPT, Gemini, and Claude compared through real projects, not demos. What each one gets right, where they stumble, and how to work with them.</p>
        <a class="read" href="/blog/building-websites-with-ai">Read the post &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="post-card">
        <div class="pdate">Origin story</div>
        <h3><a href="/blog/why-blueyucca-exists">Why BlueYucca exists</a></h3>
        <p>A domain bought in 2006, a FrontPage 2003 experiment on a modern network, and an honest look at why small businesses keep paying rent on websites.</p>
        <a class="read" href="/blog/why-blueyucca-exists">Read the post &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:22px;"><a href="/blog/">See all posts</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Why this exists</div>
    <h2>Locked in a platform is not ownership. <mark>That is rent.</mark></h2>
    <div class="why reveal">
      <p>I have watched too many small business owners get pulled into website builders that start cheap and friendly, then keep finding new ways to charge once everything is locked inside. Your photos, your words, your customer links, all held on a platform you cannot leave without starting over.</p>
      <p>A simple business website does not need a platform. It needs a handful of HTML files that belong to you. Files you can host anywhere, move anytime, and hand to any helper, human or AI, without asking permission. That is what BlueYucca is here to help you build.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">The honest numbers</div>
    <h2>What it takes to own your site.</h2>
    <div class="stats reveal">
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">$0</div><strong>To build and publish</strong><p>The templates, the prompt builder, and free hosting options cost nothing.</p></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">1</div><strong>File per page</strong><p>Each page is one self-contained HTML file. Nothing hidden, nothing extra.</p></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">100%</div><strong>Yours</strong><p>Your files sit on your computer. Host them anywhere, leave anytime.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Start here</div>
    <h2>Start with a real example.</h2>
    <p class="sub">These templates are modeled on live, working sites. Pick the one closest to what you need, download it, and make it yours.</p>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/examples">Browse examples and templates</a>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Common questions</div>
    <h2>The things people ask first.</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need to know how to code?</summary>
      <p>No. You describe your business in plain words, the AI writes the file, and you save it. If you can write an email and save a file, you can do this. Over time you may start recognizing bits of the HTML, and that is a bonus, not a requirement.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What does this cost?</summary>
      <p>BlueYucca is free. The AI tools have free tiers that are enough for a simple site. Hosting can be free too, or a few dollars a month if you want extras. The hosting guide walks through both.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What is the catch?</summary>
      <p>There is none, and that is the point. BlueYucca is a free project from Cultivatum LLC built out of a conviction that small businesses should own their websites. Nothing here asks you to sign up, and the only measurement is a privacy-first counter that does not use cookies or track who you are. If you ever want my personal attention on your specific business, that is paid work and it lives at <a href="https://kakt.ai">kakt.ai</a>. Everything here stays free either way.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will the AI get it right the first time?</summary>
      <p>Sometimes yes, sometimes it takes a few tries. Results vary between Claude, ChatGPT, and Gemini, and even between days with the same tool. That is normal. Ask for changes in plain words and it will revise, just like a helpful contractor.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

