    <h2>About BlueYucca.</h2>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-main">
        <p>BlueYucca is a free, open source utility lab from Cultivatum LLC and part of the <a href="https://kakt.ai">kakt.ai</a> family. The whole point is simple: help small businesses and everyday people build websites they actually own, so nobody gets taken advantage of by rising subscriptions or platform lock-in.</p>
        <h3>How this started</h3>
        <p>Earlier this year I ran a fun test. I built a page for this domain in Microsoft FrontPage 2003, a website tool from more than two decades ago, and put it live on a modern global network. It loaded fast, it worked everywhere, and it needed no platform, no subscription, and no rebuild.</p>
        <p>That little experiment gave me the push to go back to the basics: simple, lightweight HTML that belongs to you. <a href="/frontpage/"><strong>See the original FrontPage experiment</strong></a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="funfact">
        <div class="tag">FUN FACT</div>
        <h3>Why "BlueYucca"?</h3>
        <p>No brand agency, no focus group. I just like blue yucca plants. They are one of my favorites, and I liked the way the name sounded. So I bought the domain back in 2006, and then it sat there for twenty years, waiting for a purpose. It finally has one.</p>
